KG42.register("slice-clusters-54dbf093a399f36099561029",{"id":"50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v142-d-K001","paper":"50-residential_commercial_multi_energy","title":"Fair electricity and heat pricing, exchange decisions, and payment accounting","source_pointer":"/clusters/199","node_ids":["COMP-43c104c63456653a","COMP-d7d3d1d666d18212","COMP-5758c3aa27307ed1","COMP-739917e3869e45a6"],"rule_refs":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R001","50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R003","50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R005","50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R002"],"visible_rule_refs":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R001","50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R003","50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R005","50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R002"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[{"global_edge_id":"S-a4257216708afc86","source":"COMP-5758c3aa27307ed1","target":"COMP-739917e3869e45a6","type":"links","assertion_ids":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001"],"rule_refs":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R005"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-ba7827695ed95a8d","source":"COMP-d7d3d1d666d18212","target":"COMP-739917e3869e45a6","type":"links","assertion_ids":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E002"],"rule_refs":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R005"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-82f6f770291c2a18","source":"COMP-5758c3aa27307ed1","target":"COMP-d7d3d1d666d18212","type":"conditional_on","assertion_ids":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001"],"rule_refs":["50-residential_commercial_multi_energy::v141-c-R002"],"internal":false}],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::x::x_electricity_trading_price","v141-c-R003::x::x_heat_trading_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g03-e08","v141-b-g04-e04"],"rationale":"The same model simultaneously determines exchange and fair prices, and the source text attributes transaction-price optimization to a Nash-type objective. Here only a functional coupling is established; no new scientific edge that clearing precedes pricing is added, nor are missing cost equations supplied."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_heat_trading_price","v141-c-R003::x::x_electricity_trading_price"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x01","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x02","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e10","v141-b-g04-e03","v141-b-g04-e04","v141-b-g04-e06"],"rationale":"The unified electricity and heat prices in the pricing Rule-Chain are exactly the unit prices used in the payment equations of both parties, and A11/A12 further state that they use the same transaction prices as A7/A8. The two local roles of pricing decision and payment input are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Ector","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-Ertoc","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-QctorHeat","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-QrtocHeat"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-E-ctor","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-E-rtoc","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Q-ctor-heat","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Q-rtoc-heat"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e11","v141-b-g04-e15","v141-b-g04-e16"],"rationale":"The terminology definitions and A21–A23 support the electricity and heat exchange quantities with the same direction and same index appearing respectively in the allocation and execution constraints; this is a quantity interface, not newly added execution timing."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-e15"],"rationale":"R001 combines A21a–A22c into one item, while R002 carries the four exchange-coupling inequalities and the two purchase-sale state restrictions separately. These correspond to different groupings of the same set of grid constraints and cannot be regarded as three independent newly added obligations or as equivalence of the entire Rule-Chain."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Q-ctor-heat","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-Q-rtoc-heat","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-E-ctor","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-E-rtoc"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x03","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x04","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x05","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x06","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e11","v141-b-g04-e03","v141-b-g04-e06","v141-b-g04-e15","v141-b-g04-e16"],"rationale":"The directed exchange quantities of the two entities in the execution constraints enter the aggregation and payment of the settlement Rule-Chain. The heat supplied between commercial buildings does not belong to this payment interface, and the hourly quantity is not directly equated with its aggregate quantity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x11","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x12","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-RAC","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-CAC","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g04-e06"],"rationale":"The supplied cost definition includes transaction payments and revenues in annualized costs, and the costs then form the profit objective, supporting the functional association. The frozen Rule-Chain lacks these cost equations, and the positive/negative signs in the citation have semantic doubts, so this mapping only identifies an interface awaiting closure."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
